  "name": "Kemocon",
  "shortName": null,
  "description": "Kemocon, a blend of \"kemono\" and \"convention\", is a furry convention in Japan and the second furry convention series in the country. It was the only one running after TransFur ended in 2007 and before Fur-st began in 2011. The first was held November 30, 2008, at the Kawasaki City Industrial Promotion Hall in Kawasaki, and it has since moved to Sumida in Tokyo, Kisarazu in Chiba and the Osanbashi Yokohama International Passenger Terminal. It grew from a one-day event to a two-day event in 2014, and is organized by the Kemocon Organizing Committee Team.",
